  <body>
    <outline text="November 2026" type="calendarMonth" date="2026-11">
      <outline text="27th November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-27">
        <outline text="Daily notes in TheBrain ![Here's my brain today](/images/2026/11/thebrain-full-27155838.webp)" created="Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:58:02 GMT">
          <outline text="I love this thing. The recent addition of a local API has really made things easy. I can put _everything_ in there." created="Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:00:00 GMT"/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="I started a &quot;Journal&quot; over on the new (to me) [Wordwrap.lol](https://wordwrap.lol) from the [omg.lol](https://omg.lol) folks. Because I'm unlikely to commit, I kept it at their subdomain: [jbaty.wordwrap.lol](https://jbaty.wordwrap.lol). I don't know what it's for. ¯\_(ツ)_/¯" created="Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:01:20 GMT"/>
      </outline>
      <outline text="26th November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-26">
        <outline text="Playing with [orgstar](https://krz.sh/apps/orgstar/), a Mac/iPhone app for org mode files. It's a little buggy, but the idea is spot on. We need more of this kind of thing." created="Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:14:04 GMT"/>
        <outline text="This is a test from the Framework to see if I can post here from different machines. It should be a matter of connecting with a token and reloading. Seems to have worked. If you're reading this, it has." created="Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:04:09 GMT"/>
        <outline text="It occurred to me that I have no idea how [Porridge](https://github.com/alexjj/porridge) works. Do I care? I mean, I don't know how my phone works. Or GPS. Or, hell, my microwave. Does it matter?" created="Thu, 26 Nov 2026 11:07:55 GMT"/>
      </outline>
      <outline text="25th November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-25">
        <outline text="Dull Grey" created="Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:29:14 GMT">
          <outline text="&gt; ...the dull grey of what everyone at a particular period might repeat -- Foucault" created="Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:29:26 GMT"/>
          <outline text="This is how I feel about my Mastodon feed"/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="I am never going to learn how to stay away from screens. My phone isn't a problem, but the Mac on my desk absorbs nearly all of my time. It's not good for me, but no matter where I am or what I'm doing, I just want to get back to the computer." created="Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:53:53 GMT"/>
      </outline>
      <outline text="24th November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-24">
        <outline text="Sometimes I just want to type and click publish using an outliner. Guess what, you're soaking in it." created="Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:54:51 GMT"/>
      </outline>
      <outline text="22nd November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-22">
        <outline text="The anticipation of the new camera arriving is blocking my view of everything this morning. " created="Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:00:59 GMT"/>
      </outline>
      <outline text="21st November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-21">
        <outline text="The X100VI is now scheduled to arrive tomorrow. Will that leave me enough time to watch every video and read every blog post about the camera first?" created="Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:54:18 GMT"/>
      </outline>
      <outline text="20th November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-20">
        <outline text="![Self-portrait with the 24+ year old Canon EOS-1Ds](/images/2026/11/20261120-00581-20160018.webp)" created="Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:59:47 GMT"/>
        <outline text="It's a new day and porridge knows it. Clicking a button to have a site rendered for me without ongoing hassle is kind of nice." created="Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:58:23 GMT"/>
      </outline>
      <outline text="19th November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-19">
        <outline text="[Paul Ford (NYT)](https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/30/opinion/anthropic-ipo-ai.html)" created="Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:21:56 GMT">
          <outline text="&quot;As much as I love computers, democracy is the more important technology.&quot;"/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="A new leaf" created="Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:37:57 GMT">
          <outline text="![Me holding a giant leaf I found while walking Alice this morning](/images/2026/11/20261119-00547-19173934.webp)" created="Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:38:02 GMT"/>
          <outline text="This is just my way of exercising Porridge. Still, it's a neat leaf, right?"/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="What did I write?" created="Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:07:23 GMT">
          <outline text="![Missing pages](/images/2026/11/mead-pad-19170807.webp)" created="Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:08:33 GMT"/>
          <outline text="Probably something brilliant. Gone now, though ¯\_(ツ)_/¯"/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="Goldilocks' lunch" created="Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:00:19 GMT">
          <outline text="That's right, it's [porridge: A blogging platform](https://github.com/alexjj/porridge). Now what, Alex?" created="Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:00:43 GMT"/>
        </outline>
      </outline>
    </outline>
  </body>
